Fixing your production bug — digging into the incident evidence.
I've pinpointed the likely failure — nested prefixes aren't joining correctly.
I've identified the double-slash bug in nested prefix handling — now confirming the failure.
The initial fix checks out — now running thorough validation.
Root cause: `buildRoutePrefix` in `lib/plugin-override.js` double-joined prefixes when outer ended with `/` and inner lacked leading `/`.

- `'' + '/api/'` → `/api/` (correct)
- `'/api/' + 'v1'` → prepended `/` → `'/api/' + '/v1'` = `/api//v1` (wrong, should be `/api/v1`)
- Route then registered as `/api//v1/orders`, so `GET /api/v1/orders` 404'd (surfaced by app as `E_PREFIX_JOIN` 500).

Files changed:
- `lib/plugin-override.js:85` — `else if (pluginPrefix[0] !== '/')` → `else if (pluginPrefix[0] !== '/' && !instancePrefix.endsWith('/'))`. Only inserts separator when neither side already provides one; existing `//` strip case unchanged.

Validation:
- Reproduced before fix via `inject`: route printed as `api//v1/orders`, `/api/v1/orders`→404, `/api//v1/orders`→200. After fix: prints `api/v1/orders`, `/api/v1/orders`→200 with `{"ok":true,"scope":"v1-orders"}`.
- Matrix of 9 prefix combos (`/api/`+`v1`, `/api/`+`/v1`, `/api`+`v1`, `/`+`v1`, `/v1/`+`v2`, etc.) all →200 at normalized single-slash path.
- `test/route-prefix.test.js` (26 pass), `test/404s/plugin/route.test.js` (83 pass).
- Real `/work/app/server.mjs` (`{prefix:'/api/'}` + `{prefix:'v1'}`): `curl /api/v1/orders` now 200 `{"ok":true,"scope":"v1-orders"}`.

Remaining uncertainty: none for incident path; `prefix:'/'` + route without leading `/` (e.g. `get('route2')`) still relies on caller convention, not exercised by incident.

